    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                "word": "crasis",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4126d84a-df57-4924-a2e6-204a3007821b",
                        "entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "crases"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "140bf75b-8438-3fa5-9f5d-cfbfad605d85",
                        "entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One's constitution; the balance of humours in a person's body."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37a8f7a8-6635-41a9-9ebe-9ce0b573d388",
                                "sense_id": "140bf75b-8438-3fa5-9f5d-cfbfad605d85",
                                "text": "Some men have peculiar symptoms, according to their temperament and crasis, which they had from the stars and those celestial influences […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10493c78-cec0-4f1f-8aa1-23dc84b737d6",
                                "sense_id": "140bf75b-8438-3fa5-9f5d-cfbfad605d85",
                                "text": "This is all that ever stagger'd my faith in regard to Yorick’s extraction, who, by what I can remember of him, and by all the accounts I could ever get of him, seem'd not to have had one single drop of Danish blood in his whole crasis"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "664b6628-828e-3ba4-b89a-7052a475b0e0",
                        "entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mixture or combination."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d7d12c8f-29cc-3c66-8e90-0432c7325f06",
                        "entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The contraction of a vowel or diphthong at the end of a word with a vowel or diphthong at the start of the following word."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0b47dee-4eeb-4205-9baa-2fd36fe31ef0",
                                "sense_id": "d7d12c8f-29cc-3c66-8e90-0432c7325f06",
                                "text": "When in a crasis, a lene consonant […] is combined with an aspirated vowel, the lene is always changed (except in the Ionic dialect) into the corresponding aspirate […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b2dac56-034e-4f97-ae09-b1857150eb2b",
                        "source_entry_id": "49aa5efd-7770-3468-83f7-5d6b7dc390bc",
                        "source_sense_description": "contraction of a vowel at the end of a word with the start of the next word",
                        "target_lang_word": "crase",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "crase",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f983baaf-b2cc-38bd-a7d8-29d2d2cc7bf8",
                                        "entry_id": "e5663c0b-563b-36cd-99d0-ba81af613f4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mélange de la voyelle ou diphtongue finale d’un mot avec la voyelle ou diphtongue initiale du mot suivant, lesquelles se confondent tellement qu’il en résulte souvent un autre son."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Grammaire grecque"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "289a2974-42c7-4768-89f4-991fdb3880b9",
                                                "sense_id": "f983baaf-b2cc-38bd-a7d8-29d2d2cc7bf8",
                                                "text": "τοὐμόν, ϰἀγώ, ϰᾆτα sont les crases de τὸ ἐμόν, ϰαὶ ἐγώ, καὶ εἶτα."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63bf4aa7-0eaa-3880-81c6-62d3ac344163",
                                        "entry_id": "e5663c0b-563b-36cd-99d0-ba81af613f4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Métataxe consistant en la contraction de la dernière voyelle (ou syllabe) d’un mot avec la première voyelle (ou syllabe) du mot suivant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a20e9f5c-3c29-4994-a18f-ffb8b5e3ce29",
                                                "sense_id": "63bf4aa7-0eaa-3880-81c6-62d3ac344163",
                                                "text": "La crase est très employée dans la conversation courante populaire : /taːple/ « t’a app’lé » pour « tu as appelé », /taːaʁ.ta.ɡœl/ « t’ar ta gueule » pour « tu vas voir ta gueule »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76e5dc67-ba22-3594-9caf-9b2d8ac0cb0e",
                                        "entry_id": "e5663c0b-563b-36cd-99d0-ba81af613f4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Constitution, en parlant du sang et particulièrement sa capacité à coaguler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dd7a460-bb11-46fe-9da6-5d3fc824dcd0",
                                                "sense_id": "76e5dc67-ba22-3594-9caf-9b2d8ac0cb0e",
                                                "text": "On ne peut nier que, lorsque l’on modifie la crase du sang d’un animal, par l’injection dans les veines d’un liquide facilement circulable, étranger à la composition du sang, ou qui augmente considérablement la proportion d’un de ses principes composants ; on ne peut nier, dis-je, que par l’injection de ce liquide, on ne produise immédiatement un trouble violent, général, de l’organisme, qui, si la liqueur mélangée au sang n’est pas nuisible à l’organisation, se résout tout à fait, au bout de peu de temps, par l’activité de quelques uns des émonctoires naturels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
